1
00:04:47,368 --> 00:04:53,368
The legend no one can forget has become the greatest 3D adventure ever filmed.

2
00:09:34,736 --> 00:09:40,736
Ghosts of the Abyss is a documentary film directed by James Cameron.

3
00:14:22,105 --> 00:14:28,105
With a team of the world's foremost historic and marine experts as well as friend Bill Paxton, James Cameron embarks on an
unscripted adventure back to the wreck of the Titanic where nearly 1,500 souls lost their lives almost a century ago.

4
00:19:09,473 --> 00:19:15,473
Self, played by Bill Paxton.

5
00:23:56,842 --> 00:24:02,842
Self, played by John Broadwater.

6
00:28:44,210 --> 00:28:50,210
Self, played by James Cameron.

7
00:33:31,578 --> 00:33:37,578
Self, played by Charles Pellegrino.

8
00:38:18,947 --> 00:38:24,947
Self, played by Lewis Abernathy.

9
00:43:06,315 --> 00:43:12,315
Self, played by Mike Cameron.

10
00:47:53,684 --> 00:47:59,684
Ghosts of the Abyss (also known as Titanic 3D: Ghosts of the Abyss) is a 2003 American documentary film
directed by James Cameron and produced by Walden Media about the wreck of the RMS Titanic.

11
00:52:41,052 --> 00:52:47,052
It was directed by James Cameron after his 1997 film Titanic.

12
00:57:28,421 --> 00:57:34,421
In August and September 2001, Cameron and a group of
scientists staged an expedition to the Titanic wreck.

13
01:02:15,789 --> 01:02:21,789
They dived in Russian deep submersibles to obtain more
detailed images than anyone had before.

14
01:07:03,157 --> 01:07:09,157
Using two small, purpose-built remotely operated vehicles, the documentary offers glimpses into the
wreck and, with CGI, superimposes the ship's original appearance on the deep-dive images.

15
01:11:50,526 --> 01:11:56,526
The film is narrated by Bill Paxton, who joined Cameron on the expedition
and played Brock Lovett in Cameron's 1997 film Titanic.

16
01:16:37,894 --> 01:16:43,894
The film premiered for IMAX 3D and was nominated for
a BFCA award for Best Documentary.

17
01:21:25,263 --> 01:21:31,263
The submersibles Mir 1 and Mir 2 carried the filming team on 12 dives.

18
01:26:12,631 --> 01:26:18,631
The film explores themes of diving, shipwreck,
titanic, underwater, oceanic expedition.
